tScality/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JeanMarcMilletScality/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JeanMarcMilletScality/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/JeanMarcMilletScality","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scality/zenko-ui/commits/7ab2dc0501ac14da7c3cad097c045d04eeb2ef11/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-23T15:38:29Z","email":"jean-marc.millet@scality.com","name":"Jean-Marc Millet"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-23T15:38:29Z","email":"jean-marc.millet@scality.com","name":"Jean-Marc Millet"},"message":"chore(responsive): prune the comments this branch added (ARTESCA-17790)\n\nAn independent pass over every comment block the branch added, judged against\nthe scaffolding criteria: a comment may hold provenance, a workaround, a\nload-bearing declaration or a counter-intuitive constraint, and nothing else.\n\nCut seven blocks that argued a design decision rather than recording one --\nwhich column takes the slack, which action sits where, why a floor exists --\nand one restatement of the \"one cellStyle serves both header and body\" rule\nalready stated in full at its least guessable site. Trimmed thirteen more to\nthe clause that carried the meaning, chiefly the flex automatic-minimum-size\nmechanism, which was explained four times over.\n\nComment density across the branch: 90 lines per 695 of code before, 65 per 640\nafter.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"159b83e1c381da3ecc1c065dd7857ea111fac2c0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scality/zenko-ui/git/trees/159b83e1c381da3ecc1c065dd7857ea111fac2c0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scality/zenko-ui/git/commits/7ab2dc0501ac14da7c3cad097c045d04eeb2ef11","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"ht