"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/download-helper/commits/a033d72b610266ebbd2a2cc1ccf9917c0c1b1ff3/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-20T07:07:48Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSÉ"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-20T07:07:48Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"chore: harden download-helper (security, a11y AAA, quality, tests) (#19)\n\n* chore: harden download-helper (security, a11y AAA, quality, tests)\n\nBlind multi-level review (architecture, security, code quality, ergonomy,\naccessibility AAA, test coverage, documentation) and remediation.\n\nSecurity\n- Block IPv6 unique-local (fc00::/7) in the SSRF guard (Java''s\n  isSiteLocalAddress only covers the deprecated fec0::/10).\n- Enforce a download byte-cap in copyWithLimit on BOTH branches so a server\n  advertising a small Content-Length but streaming more cannot fill the disk.\n- Sanitize url/filename/user before they enter email subject/body (CRLF /\n  content injection); validate ccEmail format before forwarding to the mailer.\n- Replace the ReDoS-prone email regex with a linear, backtracking-safe one.\n\nCorrectness / quality (Java)\n- Fix FTP URLConnection leak on the insufficient-space early return.\n- Reject whitespace-only filenames in DownloadPaths (isBlank).\n- Extract ensureDownloadFolder (dedup activate/download); the read-only query\n  no longer mutates the filesystem. Validate protocol early; narrow catches.\n- Bundle-managed ExecutorService for downloads with @Deactivate shutdown\n  (was an untracked raw Thread). MailService via BundleUtils (not Spring).\n- Reduce cognitive complexity of download()/downloadHttps below threshold;\n  add DownloadHelperConstants.PERMISSION; @Component service attr; minor cleanups.\n\nFrontend / ergonomy / accessibility (WCAG 2.2 AAA)\n- Add the missing root .eslintrc.js (yarn lint was broken) + strip-ansi\n  resolutions so the default formatter works.\n- Remove console.debug; one-time/robust focus handling; handle the files-query\n  error; explicit success check; clear form on success; restore document.title.\n- Accessible <dialog> delete confirmation (replaces window.confirm); per-row\n  delete state; AAA contrast; 44px targets; <output> polite live regions;\n  <section aria-labelledby> root; reduced-motion; remove duplicate aria-labels.\n- Decompose the monolithic component into PropTyped sub-components.\n- Add de/fr locales (was English-only).\n\nTests\n- 2 -> 112 Java tests (SSRF incl. fc00::/7 + IPv4-mapped + numeric forms,\n  path-traversal incl. whitespace, FileSizeUtils, service protocol/validation)\n  + 13 Jest/RTL tests. Cypress: de-brittle Moonstone selectors, fix the\n  download race, add mutation/query permission-deny tests.\n\nBuild / docs\n- Sync package.json version to pom (2.0.6-SNAPSHOT); add SonarQube properties;\n  correct AGENTS.md (adminDownloadHelper permission, executor lifecycle).\n\nSonarQube quality gate: OK (0 new issues, ratings A, 0% duplication).\nCypress: 20 passing / 0 failing.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* fix: address PR review (executor reject-guard, double-submit, a11y)\n\nBlind PR review findings:\n- Java: submitDownload now catches RejectedExecutionException so a late\n  submit racing @Deactivate cannot propagate an unchecked 500 to the client.\n- Frontend: remove a leftover console.error in the submit catch; guard the\n  delete-confirm dialog against double-submit (isConfirming state disables\n  Confirm before the dialog closes); associate the protocol hint via\n  aria-describedby; add aria-atomic to the files live region; drop the dead\n  Moonstone `hint` prop (the component uses `helper`) keeping the working\n  aria-describedby description; remove the orphaned confirmDelete i18n key.\n\nSonarQube gate OK; ESLint 0 errors; Jest 13/13; Cypress 20 passing / 0 failing.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","tree":{"sha":"ff095070bcac2a2bf49bb287d7a2eea5a68c58b9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/download-helper/git/trees/ff095070bcac2a2bf49bb287d7a2eea5a68c58b9"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/download-helper/git/commits/a033d72b610266ebbd2a2cc1ccf9917c0c1b1ff3","verification":{"payload":"tree ff095070bcac2a2bf49bb287d7a2eea5a68c58b9\nparent 312e336693d12ac51432eecc56c44a05d4c04a83\nauthor Florent BOURASSÉ <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1781939268 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781939268 +0200\n\nchore: harden download-helper (security, a11y AAA, quality, tests) (#19)\n\n* chore: harden download-helper (security, a11y AAA, quality, tests)\n\nBlind multi-level review (architecture, security, code quality, ergonomy,\naccessibility AAA, test coverage, documentation) and remediation.\n\nSecurity\n- Block IPv6 unique-local (fc00::/7) in the SSRF guard (Java''s\n  isSiteLocalAddress only covers the deprecated fec0::/10).\n- Enforce a download byte-cap in copyWithLimit on BOTH branches so a server\n  advertising a small Content-Length but streaming more cannot fill the disk.\n- Sanitize url/filename/user before they enter email subject/body (CRLF /\n  content injection); validate ccEmail format before forwarding to the mailer.\n- Replace the ReDoS-prone email regex with a linear, backtracking-safe one.\n\nCorrectness / quality (Java)\n- Fix FTP URLConnection leak on the insufficient-space early return.\n- Reject whitespace-only filenames in DownloadPaths (isBlank).\n- Extract ensureDownloadFolder (dedup activate/download); the read-only query\n  no longer mutates the filesystem. Validate protocol early; narrow catches.\n- Bundle-managed ExecutorService for downloads with @Deactivate shutdown\n  (was an untracked raw Thread). MailService via BundleUtils (not Spring).\n- Reduce cognitive complexity of download()/downloadHttps below threshold;\n  add DownloadHelperConstants.PERMISSION; @Component service attr; minor cleanups.\n\nFrontend / ergonomy / accessibility (WCAG 2.2 AAA)\n- Add the missing root .eslintrc.js (yarn lint was broken) + strip-ansi\n  resolutions so the default formatter works.\n- Remove console.debug; one-time/robust focus handling; handle the files-query\n  error; explicit success check; clear form on success; restore document.title.\n- Accessible <dialog> delete confirmation (replaces window.confirm); per-row\n  delete state; AAA contrast; 44px targets; <output> polite live regions;\n  <section aria-labelledby> root; reduced-motion; remove duplicate aria-labels.\n- Decompose the monolithic component into PropTyped sub-components.\n- Add de/fr locales (was English-only).\n\nTests\n- 2 -> 112 Java tests (SSRF incl. fc00::/7 + IPv4-mapped + numeric forms,\n  path-traversal incl. whitespace, FileSizeUtils, service protocol/validation)\n  + 13 Jest/RTL tests. Cypress: de-brittle Moonstone selectors, fix the\n  download race, add mutation/query permission-deny tests.\n\nBuild / docs\n- Sync package.json version to pom (2.0.6-SNAPSHOT); add SonarQube properties;\n  correct AGENTS.md (adminDownloadHelper permission, executor lifecycle).\n\nSonarQube quality gate: OK (0 new issues, ratings A, 0% duplication).\nCypress: 20 passing / 0 failing.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* fix: address PR review (executor reject-guard, double-submit, a11y)\n\nBlind PR review findings:\n- Java: submitDownload now catches RejectedExecutionException so a late\n  submit racing @Deactivate cannot propagate an unchecked 500 to the client.\n- Frontend: remove a leftover console.error in the submit catch; guard the\n  delete-confirm dialog against double-submit (isConfirming state disables\n  Confirm before the dialog closes); associate the protocol hint via\n  aria-describedby; add aria-atomic to the files live region; drop the dead\n  Moonstone `hint` prop (the component uses `helper`) keeping the working\n  aria-describedby description; remove the orphaned confirmDelete i18n key.\n\nSonarQube gate OK; ESLint 0 errors; Jest 13/13; Cypress 20 passing / 0 failing.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqNjxECRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAdNIQAKrD+gceFQl8ibsULKohtQtL\neFeE0U++lmhiBY+5CtaoBX/87J+FR5EIMUZI5ssr8jHVjM1W46GAD0OPygIa7og+\nscHF7DZAet0NCY2IpHfd0TIQKIWx5nO3Dh4YM5IG6OGG89VOpdnXb9BqsbLwJe2c\nuK1gZG3Opvuy9dD63E+FWmtgZLVCoui9PpJXogmJmeocQDFEw/izkp5TjIqQzYZV\n/uyxxtKsLxZ4j8gN4r1hvzaYgDXclEom+kpH6hbiNiWr3Vljb6BJTH/sp6FjhOVt\nZdzgz1M0/v9aTSXuwOph3/CRJ5E+qo3b35lxdZovHuKvsOW5HIEudi+9R4jRpl2q\n6LB2cLAhMl0klbDb3l9vhnN0vMYE3OHcBrFSki0LXBGu+bel87NHpMcFVxX35Jk+\nD0BCgZxlZnmGY4tQB4kmIdm5J7r4zqSA92esNPul2HX92QqRCmAoXTAOWXSmZ5ql\nqWMDW/RRWEuDuQ7CRlsyWcAqzDYkU+Y5xWUiWhQdn2cy52rcmVc3APxGSlIs5ZzS\nK5aV7FrFp4DzUAU5Cii3sLF00fXZOzmiZ8gs3Dh6azlRQ/k4avCE5Dz8WGGPBrvD\nAah2Eqvcu24moA+K+3jMoyyU1+F5oGGNsayopHMg5ViBqFi1IZA2BQmLwFVPCD3E\n6KveL+ZkNZiKEUtvhTvX\n=2kMj\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-06-20T07:07:49Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/download-helper/commit/a033d72b610266ebbd2a2cc1ccf9917c0c1b1ff3","node_id":"C_kwDODoP2OdoAKGEwMzNkNzJiNjEwMjY2ZWJiZDJhMmNjMWNjZjk5MTdjMGMxYjFmZjM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/download-helper/commit/312e336693d12ac51432eecc56c44a05d4c04a83","sha":"312e336693d12ac51432eecc56c44a05d4c04a83","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/download-helper/commits/312e336693d12ac51432eecc56c44a05d4c04a83"}],"sha":"a033d72b610266ebbd2a2cc1ccf9917c0c1b1ff3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/download-helper/commits/a033d72b610266ebbd2a2cc1ccf9917c0c1b1ff3"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/download-helper/commits/312e336693d12ac51432eecc56c44a05d4c04a83/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-10T19:06:53Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSÉ"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-10T19:06:53Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"test: fine-grained permission regression tests + assignable admin role (#18)\n\n* feat: replace adminSystemInfos with module-specific adminDownloadHelper permission\n\nDefine jnt:permission adminDownloadHelper (child of admin) in\nsrc/main/import/permissions.xml so it is packaged into import.zip\nby the Jahia Maven plugin. Replace all four @GraphQLRequiresPermission\nannotations in DownloadHelperMutationExtension and\nDownloadHelperQueryExtension.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* fix: update requiredPermission to module-specific permission in frontend registration\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* test: add fine-grained permission regression tests + assignable admin role\n\nAdd regression coverage for the fine-grained `adminDownloadHelper`\npermission so the gate cannot be silently removed or mismatched across\nthe stack (GraphQL annotation, admin-route requiredPermission, RBAC role).\n\n- src/main/import/roles.xml: ship an assignable `download-helper-administrator`\n  server role granting ONLY `administrationAccess adminDownloadHelper` — no\n  full `admin`. `administrationAccess` is required so the admin UI renders.\n- tests/cypress/e2e/02-downloadHelper-Permissions.cy.ts: 4 tests.\n  - GraphQL: a user without the permission is denied the gated\n    `downloadHelperInfo` query (Permission denied); a user granted only the\n    module role gets full success (data returned, no errors).\n  - Admin UI: the panel is hidden for the denied user and visible for the\n    granted user at /jahia/administration/downloadHelper.\n- pom.xml: bump module version 2.0.5 -> 2.0.6-SNAPSHOT so the import content\n  (roles.xml) re-imports on deploy.\n\nNo inner hardcoded `admin` check existed in the resolvers (only the\n`@GraphQLRequiresPermission(\"adminDownloadHelper\")` annotation), so no Java\nrelaxation was needed; the allow path asserts full success.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","tree":{"sha":"59ed53a49ed8bc4654a89156289a4b69fc959141","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/download-helper/git/trees/59ed53a49ed8bc4654a89156289a4b69fc959141"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/download-helper/git/commits/312e336693d12ac51432eecc56c44a05d4c04a83","verification":{"payload":"tree 59ed53a49ed8bc4654a89156289a4b69fc959141\nparent 84b5760a990874c06587581f6a19310ea6811680\nauthor Florent BOURASSÉ <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1781118413 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781118413 +0200\n\ntest: fine-grained permission regression tests + assignable admin role (#18)\n\n* feat: replace adminSystemInfos with module-specific adminDownloadHelper permission\n\nDefine jnt:permission adminDownloadHelper (child of admin) in\nsrc/main/import/permissions.xml so it is packaged into import.zip\nby the Jahia Maven plugin. Replace all four @GraphQLRequiresPermission\nannotations in DownloadHelperMutationExtension and\nDownloadHelperQueryExtension.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* fix: update requiredPermission to module-specific permission in frontend registration\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* test: add fine-grained permission regression tests + assignable admin role\n\nAdd regression coverage for the fine-grained `adminDownloadHelper`\npermission so the gate cannot be silently removed or mismatched across\nthe stack (GraphQL annotation, admin-route requiredPermission, RBAC role).\n\n- src/main/import/roles.xml: ship an assignable `download-helper-administrator`\n  server role granting ONLY `administrationAccess adminDownloadHelper` — no\n  full `admin`. `administrationAccess` is required so the admin UI renders.\n- tests/cypress/e2e/02-downloadHelper-Permissions.cy.ts: 4 tests.\n  - GraphQL: a user without the permission is denied the gated\n    `downloadHelperInfo` query (Permission denied); a user granted only the\n    module role gets full success (data returned, no errors).\n  - Admin UI: the panel is hidden for the denied user and visible for the\n    granted user at /jahia/administration/downloadHelper.\n- pom.xml: bump module version 2.0.5 -> 2.0.6-SNAPSHOT so the import content\n  (roles.xml) re-imports on deploy.\n\nNo inner hardcoded `admin` check existed in the resolvers (only the\n`@GraphQLRequiresPermission(\"adminDownloadHelper\")` annotation), so no Java\nrelaxation was needed; the allow path asserts full success.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqKbXNCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAqOgQAFjZDqxaRK0F7YgjXrrY33+W\nHLPyIdUxqtgR6yLDeIYzXu9am/DCrPCSuJLcnkYJ7KrGKjYX4gIgtOlyV+vqFnr1\nm+ReNQtQYWcye28gIH+gvofZVCPkHobjixG4onBcM91xQd1KGGm6vTYA9Wpb5rHK\nuPf4QhzUrIsSG/1s3cywRqXBEjvRY2JaXInb3206EUmg3QGiB2Of1rbHq9MGSFtZ\nPDxR1ogG3ecU68H1vlHSvJe+UrA5vg+Xr8/ey4siHN0lz1ZwqQPJNY13fxTTgVYF\ntKmxteAzUgCwPLuWBwGQeAOG8nKOcgdM+Rb/cFc