ttps://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/download-helper/commit/2d7cab0b058b741f203ccb1fc8321a69e4b7251b","node_id":"C_kwDODoP2OdoAKDJkN2NhYjBiMDU4Yjc0MWYyMDNjY2IxZmM4MzIxYTY5ZTRiNzI1MWI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/download-helper/commit/8bfe621655302a226dbae2124cd9f9e687fcdd3b","sha":"8bfe621655302a226dbae2124cd9f9e687fcdd3b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/download-helper/commits/8bfe621655302a226dbae2124cd9f9e687fcdd3b"},{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/download-helper/commit/d8e68d89b9094f19f848bfc8626ebb01ecb6e1b6","sha":"d8e68d89b9094f19f848bfc8626ebb01ecb6e1b6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/download-helper/commits/d8e68d89b9094f19f848bfc8626ebb01ecb6e1b6"}],"sha":"2d7cab0b058b741f203ccb1fc8321a69e4b7251b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/download-helper/commits/2d7cab0b058b741f203ccb1fc8321a69e4b7251b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/download-helper/commits/d8e68d89b9094f19f848bfc8626ebb01ecb6e1b6/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-28T06:01:56Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSE"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-28T06:01:56Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSE"},"message":"security: harden HTTPS download against redirect-based SSRF and log injection (SECURITY-746)\n\nThe existing SSRF guard (commit 406ed1c) validated only the initial URL host;\nthe shared Apache HttpClient followed redirects automatically, letting a remote\nserver 30x-redirect to an internal / cloud-metadata host and bypass the check.\nThe same redirect would also replay the admin-supplied Basic credentials to\nthe redirect target.\n\nFixes\n- F1 (MEDIUM) SSRF guard bypass via HTTP redirects + Basic-auth credential leakage.\n  downloadHttps now disables RequestConfig.setRedirectsEnabled and follows\n  redirects manually in a bounded loop (max 5 hops). Every hop is re-validated\n  with assertSafeHost; only http(s) Location targets are honored; the\n  Authorization header is added only when the current hop is the originally\n  validated host (UrlSecurityUtils.sameHost).\n- F2 (LOW) Log injection in DownloadHelperMutationExtension.triggerDownload —\n  the async-failure log path now routes url/filename/user through\n  UrlSecurityUtils.sanitizeForLog, matching the rest of the codebase.\n\nRefactor\n- Extract pure, side-effect-free SSRF predicates into UrlSecurityUtils\n  (sanitizeForLog, isBlockedHost, isNonRoutableAddress, isRedirectStatus,\n  isAllowedHttpScheme, resolveLocation, sameHost, hostOf) so they are\n  unit-testable without DNS or OSGi.\n- DownloadHelperService.assertSafeHost now delegates to UrlSecurityUtils;\n  the BLOCKED_HOSTS set and inline private-address classification are\n  consolidated in one tested place.\n\nTests\n- 58 JUnit 5 / AssertJ tests in UrlSecurityUtilsTest covering CRLF stripping,\n  blocked hosts (case-insensitive), non-routable address classification\n  (loopback, link-local, site-local, any-local, multicast, IPv6 loopback /\n  link-local, 169.254.169.254), redirect status detection (301/302/303/307/308),\n  scheme allow-listing, relative and absolute Location resolution, and\n  same-host comparison for credential replay.\n- All 13 Cypress E2E specs pass against a live Jahia with the patched module\n  (verified end-to-end including a real redirect-following download from\n  store.jahia.com/cms/mavenproxy).\n\nResidual\n- DNS-rebinding TOCTOU between assertSafeHost resolution and the HTTP client''s\n  connect-time resolution is documented in AGENTS.md as an accepted residual;\n  fully closing it requires IP pinning via a custom connection manager,\n  disproportionate for an adminSystemInfos-gated tool.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","tree":{"sha":"f37ad83488cd62f35e8412200541c0806e03e6ad","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/download-helper/git/trees/f37ad83488cd62f35e8412200541c0806e03e6ad"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/download-helper/git/commits/d8e68d89b9094f19f848bfc8626ebb01ecb6e1b6","verification":{"payload":"tree f37ad83488cd62f35e8412200541c0806e03e6ad\nparent 8bfe621655302a226dbae2124cd9f9e687fcdd3b\nauthor Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1779948116 +0200\ncommitter Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1779948116 +0200\n\nsecurity: harden HTTPS download against redirect-based SSRF and log injection (SECURITY-746)\n\nThe existing SSRF guard (commit 406ed1c) validated only the initial URL host;\nthe shared Apache HttpClient followed redirects automatically, letting a remote\nserver 30x-redirect to an internal / cloud-metadata host and bypass the check.\nThe same redirect would also replay the admin-supplied Basic credentials to\nthe redirect target.\n\nFixes\n- F1 (MEDIUM) SSRF guard bypass via HTTP redirects + Basic-auth credential leakage.\n  downloadHttps now disables RequestConfig.setRedirectsEnabled and follows\n  redirects manually in a bounded loop (max 5 hops). Every hop is re-validated\n  with assertSafeHost; only http(s) Location targets are honored; the\n  Authorization header is added only when the current hop is the originally\n  validated host (UrlSecurityUtils.sameHost).\n- F2 (LOW) Log injection in DownloadHelperMutationExtension.triggerDownload —\n  the async-failure log path now routes url/filename/user through\n  UrlSecurityUtils.sanitizeForLog, matching the rest of the codebase.\n\nRefactor\n- Extract pure, side-effect-free SSRF predicates into UrlSecurityUtils\n  (sanitizeForLog, isBlockedHost, isNonRoutableAddress, isRedirectStatus,\n  isAllowedHttpScheme, resolveLocation, sameHost, hostOf) so they are\n  unit-testable without DNS or OSGi.\n- DownloadHelperService.assertSafeHost now delegates to UrlSecurityUtils;\n  the BLOCKED_HOSTS set and inline private-address classification are\n  consolidated in one tested place.\n\nTests\n- 58 JUnit 5 / AssertJ tests in UrlSecurityUtilsTest covering CRLF stripping,\n  blocked hosts (case-insensitive), non-routable address classification\n  (loopback, link-local, site-local, any-local, multicast, IPv6 loopback /\n  link-local, 169.254.169.254), redirect status detection (301/302/303/307/308),\n  scheme allow-listing, relative and absolute Location resolution, and\n  same-host comparison for credential replay.\n- All 13 Cypress E2E specs pass against a live Jahia with the patched module\n  (verified end-to-end including a real redirect-following download from\n  store.jahia.com/cms/mavenproxy).\n\nResidual\n- DNS-rebinding TOCTOU between assertSafeHost resolution and the HTTP client''s\n  connect-time resolution is documented in AGENTS.md as an accepted residual;\n  fully closing it requires IP pinning via a custom connection manager,\n  disproportionate for an adminSystemInfos-gated tool.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niQEzBAABCgAdFiEEtcDrrZ6KblczSEt9UhsGUDwSL3kFAmoX2lQACgkQUhsGUDwS\nL3n/+gf9G6wjEWtItFxZ6soFnru9pj/hqp34vt3p0YbVexBdyZixIrAj0iWNswFd\nrGiyVCfH3JzaTOwyMZBtaqJoFuZ4lnesuVWJ9TnrXQFO1KGTtDDbtDHss0ngGHZk\nyr+QMVQ15SvzeReTHZ7Q31kY87NIHPdAThYLeF1iAXWvjAVLHpAJPHRURfuMnOfG\nDhpnbdSTgk3opUmt821qTXzZNINJi8MYSRGBegRgeXq+k6zDVZ5l6sXd3nvdVkCG\nS5jLL1z9pjae22W9A/DUoSGD4EGiVthlDnu74ngzt+TIxuuBzboppZLHe3r/780W\n2NZlRY4xyp+ghJ9vlk/Qj5KLiMZQeA==\n=Vap1\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-05-28T06:02:03Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/user