starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ioBroker/ioBroker.cameras/commit/b08d484aa0dcbaf3bdec15bcabf01169c03a4871","node_id":"C_kwDODqs91NoAKGIwOGQ0ODRhYTBkY2JhZjNiZGVjMTViY2FiZjAxMTY5YzAzYTQ4NzE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ioBroker/ioBroker.cameras/commit/7b9d97aad19eaad7dc226568c0990fae5b94a426","sha":"7b9d97aad19eaad7dc226568c0990fae5b94a426","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.cameras/commits/7b9d97aad19eaad7dc226568c0990fae5b94a426"},{"html_url":"https://github.com/ioBroker/ioBroker.cameras/commit/c0739aab134004e54d652d75253a6574ae732482","sha":"c0739aab134004e54d652d75253a6574ae732482","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.cameras/commits/c0739aab134004e54d652d75253a6574ae732482"}],"sha":"b08d484aa0dcbaf3bdec15bcabf01169c03a4871","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.cameras/commits/b08d484aa0dcbaf3bdec15bcabf01169c03a4871"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4582016?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/GermanBluefox","id":4582016,"login":"GermanBluefox","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1ODIwMTY=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.cameras/commits/ac002b273c0036bd61ca1c91547a0b93cfe706b9/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-03T05:15:54Z","email":"dogafox@gmail.com","name":"GermanBluefox"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-03T05:15:54Z","email":"dogafox@gmail.com","name":"GermanBluefox"},"message":"Do not wake a Eufy camera for the first image at the adapter start\n\ninitLivestream() was careful not to press \"start_stream\" - but fillFiles()\nasks every camera for a picture right after the cameras are initialized, so\nevery Eufy camera without RTSP of its own was woken through its station at\nevery adapter start, and the start waited up to 45 s for it. The test that\nclaimed the opposite only called init(), never process().\n\nA camera can now say that a snapshot costs more than the request\n(wakesUpForSnapshot), and fillFiles() leaves it out - the first real request\nfetches the picture. An explicit \"running\" state still starts the stream.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"dd17179e9aaff95a6e1f2e93ff8d5b0e087ce5a3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.cameras/git/trees/dd17179e9aaff95a6e1f2e93ff8d5b0e087ce5a3"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.cameras/git/commits/ac002b273c0036bd61ca1c91547a0b93cfe706b9","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4582016?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/GermanBluefox","id":4582016,"login":"GermanBluefox","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1ODIwMTY=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ioBroker/ioBroker.cameras/commit/ac002b273c0036bd61ca1c91547a0b93cfe706b9","node_id":"C_kwDODqs91NoAKGFjMDAyYjI3M2MwMDM2YmQ2MWNhMWM5MTU0N2EwYjkzY2ZlNzA2Yjk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ioBroker/ioBroker.cameras/commit/cfc11858638e76531150181ff689bb4651333f73","sha":"cfc11858638e76531150181ff689bb4651333f73","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.cameras/commits/cfc11858638e76531150181ff689bb4651333f73"}],"sha":"ac002b273c0036bd61ca1c91547a0b93cfe706b9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.cameras/commits/ac002b273c0036bd61ca1c91547a0b93cfe706b9"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4582016?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/GermanBluefox","id":4582016,"login":"GermanBluefox","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1ODIwMTY=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.cameras/commits/cfc11858638e76531150181ff689bb4651333f73/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-03T05:15:46Z","email":"dogafox@gmail.com","name":"GermanBluefox"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-03T05:15:46Z","email":"dogafox@gmail.com","name":"GermanBluefox"},"message":"Try .png and .jpg for a manufacturer logo again\n\nThe manufacturer picker only requested <id>.svg and hid the image on error.\ntools/logos.js, however, keeps a logo that is already there whatever of\n.svg/.png/.jpg it is - and writes no monogram for that id. So a hand-made\n.png, which is the documented way to add a real logo, showed nothing at all.\n\nManufacturerIcon now walks the three extensions on error, as Universal.tsx\ndid before the picker moved into TypeSelector.tsx, and the comments in\nlogos.js and CLAUDE.md point at the new place.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"f5be40974c6c3b60ade4e1c9b1ff8bd214cf04b5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.cameras/git/trees/f5be40974c6c3b60ade4e1c9b1ff8bd214cf04b5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.cameras/git/commits/cfc11858638e76531150181ff689bb4651333f73","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4582016?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/GermanBluefox","id":4582016,"login":"GermanBluefox","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1ODIwMTY=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ioBroker/ioBroker.cameras/commit/cfc11858638e76531150181ff689bb4651333f73","node_id":"C_kwDODqs91NoAKGNmYzExODU4NjM4ZTc2NTMxMTUwMTgxZmY2ODliYjQ2NTEzMzNmNzM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ioBroker/ioBroker.cameras/commit/777be1d9265ad25eeae2aee8eb8e5dd902b0e0e7","sha":"777be1d9265ad25eeae2aee8eb8e5dd902b0e0e7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.cameras/commits/777be1d9265ad25eeae2aee8eb8e5dd902b0e0e7"}],"sha":"cfc11858638e76531150181ff689bb4651333f73","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.cameras/commits/cfc11858638e76531150181ff689bb4651333f73"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3204979?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hdering/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hdering/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hdering/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hdering/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/hdering","id":3204979,"login":"hdering","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMyMDQ5Nzk=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hdering/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hdering/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hdering/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hdering/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hdering/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hdering","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.cameras/commits/777be1d9265ad25eeae2aee8eb8e5dd902b0e0e7/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-02T10:24:01Z","email":"github@dering-online.de","name":"hdering"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-02T10:24:01Z","email":"github@dering-online.de","name":"hdering"},"message":"Reference issue #205 in the changelog\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"2c95685460d251af67b57e5c78641282d8f2b769","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.cameras/git/trees/2c95685460d251af67b57e5c78641282d8f2b769"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.cameras/git/commits/777be1d9265ad25eeae2aee8eb8e5dd902b0e0e7","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3204979?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hdering/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hdering/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hdering/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hdering/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/hdering","id":3204979,"login":"hdering","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMyMDQ5Nzk=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hdering/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hdering/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hdering/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hdering/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hdering/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hdering","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ioBroker/ioBroker.cameras/commit/777be1d9265ad25eeae2aee8eb8e5dd902b0e0e7","node_id":"C_kwDODqs91NoAKDc3N2JlMWQ5MjY1YWQyNWVlYWUyYWVlOGViOGU1ZGQ5MDJiMGUwZTc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ioBroker/ioBroker.cameras/commit/407bf8f6fe0e7b7e1dbf3fd3db9fea8944f5d7c3","sha":"407bf8f6fe0e7b7e1dbf3fd3db9fea8944f5d7c3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.cameras/commits/407bf8f6fe0e7b7e1dbf3fd3db9fea8944f5d7c3"}],"sha":"777be1d9265ad25eeae2aee8eb8e5dd902b0e0e7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.cameras/commits/777be1d9265ad25eeae2aee8eb8e5dd902b0e0e7"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3204979?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hdering/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hdering/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hdering/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hdering/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/hdering","id":3204979,"login":"hdering","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMyMDQ5Nzk=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hdering/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hdering/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hdering/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hdering/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hdering/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hdering","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.cameras/commits/407bf8f6fe0e7b7e1dbf3fd3db9fea8944f5d7c3/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-02T10:18:19Z","email":"github@dering-online.de","name":"hdering"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-02T10:18:19Z","email":"github@dering-online.de","name":"hdering"},"message":"List the cameras of eusec and stream Eufy cameras without RTSP through the station\n\nThe Eufy dialog only took an object ID, typed in or picked in the\ngeneric object browser.\n\n- With eusec installed, the dialog lists its cameras and doorbells by\n  their names from the Eufy app, and a new camera starts in that mode.\n- eusec creates rtsp_stream and rtsp_stream_url only for cameras with\n  RTSP of their own. Many battery cameras have none - they were not\n  usable at all. eusec can still stream them through the station into\n  its own go2rtc after start_stream was pressed, and then writes the\n  link to livestream_rtsp. For such a camera the adapter now presses\n  start_stream before an image, waits for the link and for the first\n  frame (up to 25 s and 20 s), and takes the snapshot from it. The\n  adapter start does not wake the camera: the address is derived from\n  the settings of eusec until the real link exists.\n- eusec deletes that link only on a regular stop. A link left behind\n  after a restart of eusec is detected by the failing snapshot, and the\n  stream is started again.\n- A missing RTSP link gives a clear error instead of \"Invalid IP\".\n- Switching between eusec and IP address was not saved, and the label\n  \"By IP address\" was never translated (the key is \"By IP Address\").\n\nThe test in the dialog waits up to 60 s longer for Eufy, starting the\nstream through the station takes that long in the worst case.\n\nTests: test/eufyLivestream.js with a simulated eusec.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"77c3e3b342389d8f2b50bb7fe81563664bf8a9e0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.cameras/git/trees/77c3e3b342389d8f2b50bb7fe81563664bf8a9e0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.cameras/git/commits/407bf8f6fe0e7b7e1dbf3fd3db9fea8944f5d7c3","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3204979?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hdering/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hdering/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hdering/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hdering/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/hdering","id":3204979,"login":"hdering","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMyMDQ5Nzk=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hdering/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hdering/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hdering/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hdering/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hdering/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hdering","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ioBroker/ioBroker.cameras/commit/407bf8f6fe0e7b7e1dbf3fd3db9fea8944f5d7c3","node_id":"C_kwDODqs91NoAKDQwN2JmOGY2ZmUwZTdiN2UxZGJmM2ZkM2RiOWZlYTg5NDRmNWQ3YzM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ioBroker/ioBroker.cameras/commit/deb89bf5524a1a419ebe8d83fa5c8c634c8e9b65","sha":"deb89bf5524a1a419ebe8d83fa5c8c634c8e9b65","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.cameras/commits/deb89bf5524a1a419ebe8d83fa5c8c634c8e9b65"}],"sha":"407bf8f6fe0e7b7e1dbf3fd3db9fea8944f5d7c3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.cameras/commits/407bf8f6fe0e7b7e1dbf3fd3db9fea8944f5d7c3"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3204979?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hdering/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hdering/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hdering/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hdering/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/hdering","id":3204979,"login":"hdering","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMyMDQ5Nzk=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hdering/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hdering/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hdering/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hdering/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hdering/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hdering","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.cameras/commits/deb89bf5524a1a419ebe8d83fa5c8c634c8e9b65/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-02T10:16:50Z","email":"github@dering-online.de","name":"hdering"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-02T10:16:50Z","email":"github@dering-online.de","name":"hdering"},"message":"Read MJPEG streams over HTTP and recognize grey H.265 snapshots\n\nMJPEG over HTTP\nAll three HTTP types (URL, URL with basic auth, model list over HTTP)\nfetched the whole response with one request. An MJPEG stream never\nends, so every such camera ran into the timeout - 477 entries of the\nmodel lists are MJPEG over HTTP.\n\nThe new src/lib/httpSnapshot.ts reads the response as a stream: a\nsingle image as before, from multipart/x-mixed-replace the first frame\n(by the Content-Length of the part if given, else up to the end marker),\nthen the connection is closed. A video stream (ASF, MP4, ...) fails at\nonce with a hint instead of a timeout. The model list offers the MJPEG\npaths again, marked as \"first frame\".\n\nGrey H.265 snapshots\nJoined between two key frames, ffmpeg decodes an H.265 frame without its\nreference picture into a flat grey area. A snapshot whose colour\nchannels have almost no deviation is taken again from a key frame\n(-skip_frame nokey), and the camera keeps that while the adapter runs.\nIf the second image is flat as well (covered lens), it is reverted - key\nframes only make every snapshot slower. \"Key frames only\" in the expert\nsettings of the RTSP type sets it permanently. The test in the dialog\nwaits twice the timeout for RTSP types, as two snapshots may be taken.\n\nTests: test/httpSnapshot.js against a local server, test/greySnapshot.js\nwith generated images instead of ffmpeg.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"beaddfbb0e7986d5acb101e36ebe1f51086e74c6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.cameras/git/trees/beaddfbb0e7986d5acb101e36ebe1f51086e74c6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.cameras/git/commits/deb89bf5524a1a419ebe8d83fa5c8c634c8e9b65","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3204979?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hdering/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hdering/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hdering/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hdering/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/hdering","id":3204979,"login":"hdering","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMyMDQ5Nzk=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hdering/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hdering/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hdering/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hdering/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hdering/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hdering","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ioBroker/ioBroker.cameras/commit/deb89bf5524a1a419ebe8d83fa5c8c634c8e9b65","node_id":"C_kwDODqs91NoAKGRlYjg5YmY1NTI0YTFhNDE5ZWJlOGQ4M2ZhNWM4YzYzNGM4ZTliNjU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ioBroker/ioBroker.cameras/commit/c0739aab134004e54d652d75253a6574ae732482","sha":"c0739aab134004e54d652d75253a6574ae732482","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.cameras/commits/c0739aab134004e54d652d75253a6574ae732482"}],"sha":"deb89bf5524a1a419ebe8d83fa5c8c634c8e9b65","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.cameras/commits/deb89bf5524a1a419ebe8d83fa5c8c634c8e9b65"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3204979?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hdering/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hdering/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hdering/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hdering/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/hdering","id":3204979,"login":"hdering","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMyMDQ5Nzk=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hdering/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hdering/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hdering/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hdering/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hdering/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hdering","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.cameras/commits/c0739aab134004e54d652d75253a6574ae732482/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-02T10:15:14Z","email":"github@dering-online.de","name":"hdering"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-02T10:15:14Z","email":"github@dering-online.de","name":"hdering"},"message":"Add cameras by manufacturer first, then the fitting connection\n\nThe type dropdown mixed protocols (URL, RTSP), single models (Reolink E1)\nand \"By manufacturer\", which opened a second manufacturer list. Many\nmanufacturers appeared twice, and it was not clear which entry to take.\n\nCamera dialog\n- The manufacturer is chosen first, \"Universal (custom URL / RTSP)\" on\n  top. Only if there are several ways to connect, a second field offers\n  them (e.g. Eufy, INSTAR, UniFi Protect next to the model list).\n- The choice maps to the existing types, so the stored configuration\n  keeps its format. Going back to the stored type in the dialog restores\n  its settings - looking at another type must not cost the API key.\n- A new camera is added through the dialog and only enters the list with\n  \"Apply\". The list shows manufacturer and connection instead of the type.\n- \"Reolink E1\" is deprecated: still supported, not offered for new\n  cameras, and converted to the Reolink model list with one click.\n\nForms\n- RTSP: one URL field instead of IP, port and path, also for rtsps://.\n  A pasted login is moved to its own fields. Transport and the ffmpeg\n  options moved to the expert settings.\n- Model list: chosen by stream path, sorted by how many models use it;\n  the model only narrows the list. HTTP paths that deliver a stream are\n  hidden - one plain request cannot read them, they always timed out.\n  The URL that will be requested is shown live. The backend accepts a\n  camera without a model now.\n- Labels for the quality selects.\n\nFixes\n- RTSP showed UDP while the adapter used TCP, and saved UDP as soon as\n  another field was changed.\n- The URL preview of an RTSP camera was only updated after saving.\n- Changes from a form were applied to the stored settings instead of the\n  edited ones, and the stream flag of the model list was set after\n  serializing, so both could get lost.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"3476a3e47de97a4029b33eb9cd8725ab83e59991","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.cameras/git/trees/3476a3e47de97a4029b33eb9cd8725ab83e59991"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.cameras/git/commits/c0739aab134004e54d652d75253a6574ae732482","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3204979?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/use