GermanBluefox) Fixed: the second viewer of the same camera did not receive any picture\n* (@GermanBluefox) Added two widgets for ioBroker.devices: RTSP camera and snapshot camera\n* (@GermanBluefox) Fixed: the `.running` state did not start or stop the stream\n* (@GermanBluefox) Fixed: width/height/angle of the `image` message were ignored\n* (@GermanBluefox) Fixed: a camera in the dialog of the snapshot widget was never used","tree":{"sha":"d996979f19a98860a4747c8678cf93cbb357ce23","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.cameras/git/trees/d996979f19a98860a4747c8678cf93cbb357ce23"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.cameras/git/commits/3437ef1e89f0495558fcebe1f48f8bfd1c273d48","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4582016?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/GermanBluefox","id":4582016,"login":"GermanBluefox","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1ODIwMTY=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ioBroker/ioBroker.cameras/commit/3437ef1e89f0495558fcebe1f48f8bfd1c273d48","node_id":"C_kwDODqs91NoAKDM0MzdlZjFlODlmMDQ5NTU1OGZjZWJlMWY0OGY4YmZkMWMyNzNkNDg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ioBroker/ioBroker.cameras/commit/8d0b6d88e249a4e260a5321818635351ced3031d","sha":"8d0b6d88e249a4e260a5321818635351ced3031d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.cameras/commits/8d0b6d88e249a4e260a5321818635351ced3031d"}],"sha":"3437ef1e89f0495558fcebe1f48f8bfd1c273d48","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.cameras/commits/3437ef1e89f0495558fcebe1f48f8bfd1c273d48"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4582016?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/GermanBluefox","id":4582016,"login":"GermanBluefox","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1ODIwMTY=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.cameras/commits/8d0b6d88e249a4e260a5321818635351ced3031d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-16T15:47:18Z","email":"dogafox@gmail.com","name":"GermanBluefox"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-16T15:47:18Z","email":"dogafox@gmail.com","name":"GermanBluefox"},"message":"Fix the errors reported in #77\n\nFive defects, all still present, found while analysing the report:\n\n- The list of allowed IPs was split with /,;/ instead of /[,;]/, so it only\n  ever split on a literal \",;\" sequence. Any list with more than one address\n  became a single bogus entry that matched nothing, and every request from a\n  non-loopback address was rejected.\n- The loopback check compared against \"::1/128\", which is CIDR notation that\n  socket.remoteAddress never returns. Connections over the IPv6 loopback\n  (\"::1\", \"::ffff:127.0.0.1\") were treated as remote.\n- Both of the above answered with \"Invalid key\" although the key was fine,\n  pointing everyone at the wrong problem. The address check now answers 403\n  \"IP not allowed\", and the key is no longer written to the log.\n- The catch around a failed image request wrote to the response without\n  checking whether it had already been sent. When the original error was\n  ERR_HTTP_HEADERS_SENT the catch threw again, escaped the async handler as an\n  unhandled rejection and terminated the adapter with code 6 - which is the\n  crash in the report.\n- The web server was started after fillFiles(), which grabs a frame from every\n  camera. With RTSP cameras that is several seconds during which everything\n  proxied to port 8200 fails with ECONNREFUSED. It now listens first.\n\nAdditionally the web extension refreshes the key by itself after a 401. It\nkeeps the copy of the instance config it was constructed with, so changing the\nkey used to break every camera until ioBroker.web was restarted as well.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"64468185b90a7a677b72e3b8ee6e8d7193c1767d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.cameras/git/trees/64468185b90a7a677b72e3b8ee6e8d7193c1767d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.cameras/git/commits/8d0b6d88e249a4e260a5321818635351ced3031d","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4582016?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/GermanBluefox","id":4582016,"login":"GermanBluefox","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1ODIwMTY=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ioBroker/ioBroker.cameras/commit/8d0b6d88e249a4e260a5321818635351ced3031d","node_id":"C_kwDODqs91NoAKDhkMGI2ZDg4ZTI0OWE0ZTI2MGE1MzIxODE4NjM1MzUxY2VkMzAzMWQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ioBroker/ioBroker.cameras/commit/9c68443edff293ffe3db646b3b4c4e396543442c","sha":"9c68443edff293ffe3db646b3b4c4e396543442c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.cameras/commits/9c68443edff293ffe3db646b3b4c4e396543442c"}],"sha":"8d0b6d88e249a4e260a5321818635351ced3031d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.cameras/commits/8d0b6d88e249a4e260a5321818635351ced3031d"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4582016?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/GermanBluefox","id":4582016,"login":"GermanBluefox","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1ODIwMTY=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.cameras/commits/9c68443edff293ffe3db646b3b4c4e396543442c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-16T13:38:32Z","email":"dogafox@gmail.com","name":"GermanBluefox"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-16T13:38:32Z","email":"dogafox@gmail.com","name":"GermanBluefox"},"message":"Do not let browsers cache snapshot responses (#68)\n\nThe snapshot route only set Content-type, so express answered with an ETag\nbut no freshness directive at all. Whether a plain <img src=\"/cameras.0/cam1\">\nrevalidates was left to the browser. Both snapshot routes now send\nCache-Control: no-store, private, the same header the MJPEG route already used.\n\nAlso documented the difference between the live route and the stored file in\nthe README. cameras.0/cam1.jpg is written once at adapter start and on every\n\"image\" message, never by requesting it, so a widget pointed at the .jpg shows\na picture that never refreshes. The two URLs differ only by the extension,\nwhich is the more likely cause of #68.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"9fc464afaa70bf64b2f7b5eb9095f1643fa03188","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.cameras/git/trees/9fc464afaa70bf64b2f7b5eb9095f1643fa03188"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.cameras/git/commits/9c68443edff293ffe3db646b3b4c4e396543442c","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4582016?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/GermanBluefox","id":4582016,"login":"GermanBluefox","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1ODIwMTY=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ioBroker/ioBroker.cameras/commit/9c68443edff293ffe3db646b3b4c4e396543442c","node_id":"C_kwDODqs91NoAKDljNjg0NDNlZGZmMjkzZmZlM2RiNjQ2YjNiNGM0ZTM5NjU0MzQ0MmM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ioBroker/ioBroker.cameras/commit/5f0bdccd15af139ec6405808f1e58876e0f91e8c","sha":"5f0bdccd15af139ec6405808f1e58876e0f91e8c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.cameras/commits/5f0bdccd15af139ec6405808f1e58876e0f91e8c"}],"sha":"9c68443edff293ffe3db646b3b4c4e396543442c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.cameras/commits/9c68443edff293ffe3db646b3b4c4e396543442c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4582016?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/GermanBluefox","id":4582016,"login":"GermanBluefox","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1ODIwMTY=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.cameras/commits/5f0bdccd15af139ec6405808f1e58876e0f91e8c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-16T12:44:57Z","email":"dogafox@gmail.com","name":"GermanBluefox"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-16T12:45:14Z","email":"dogafox@gmail.com","name":"GermanBluefox"},"message":"Fix the same incomplete lockfile in src-devices\n\nsrc-devices had the identical defect that was just fixed in src-admin:\n@rolldown/binding-wasm32-wasi declares @emnapi/core@2.0.0-alpha.3 and\n@emnapi/runtime@2.0.0-alpha.3, neither of which was resolved into the\nlockfile, so \"npm ci\" refused to install. Added both entries with the\nregistry metadata, marked dev+optional to match the surrounding tree.\n\nsrc-widgets was checked as well and is fine. All four lockfiles now pass\nboth a dependency-resolvability check and a real \"npm ci\" on linux.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"01eedbfa998fc52b8787115b30a2e62b20d2b307","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.cameras/git/trees/01eedbfa998fc52b8787115b30a2e62b20d2b307"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.cameras/git/commits/5f0bdccd15af139ec6405808f1e58876e0f91e8c","verification":{"payload":null,"reas